      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Do not increase your magnesium dosage without consulting your doctor, especially since you already have kidney concerns, as excess magnesium can be dangerous for kidneys and may cause severe side effects like vomiting or diarrhea. Your current doctor knows your specific medical history and needs to determine the safest and effective dosage for you rather than guessing online. It is possible that electrolyte imbalances or other underlying sleep issues are causing your symptoms, so a follow-up appointment might be necessary to explore better treatment options. Please contact your healthcare provider to discuss whether a supplement adjustment or alternative therapy is needed for your rest and cramps.",
